00:17:02,406 --> 00:17:04,807
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, my mind, it's this great entity.

179
00:17:05,707 --> 00:17:12,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Too personally involved, in the same sense you would be with your child, all of that results in a loss of perspective.

180
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:16,870
[SPEAKER_01]: Perspective that would be revealing the danger of that situation.

181
00:17:17,391 --> 00:17:19,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the cow herd simile in the Sutta.

182
00:17:19,251 --> 00:17:25,253
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you know, if the person responsible for keeping an eye on the cows while they're grazing,

183
00:17:26,352 --> 00:17:36,334
[SPEAKER_01]: If someone forgets that they're going to beat him and imprison him, if the cows go and eat other people's fields, he won't pay attention to where they eat and what they do.

184
00:17:37,554 --> 00:17:41,835
[SPEAKER_01]: And most people choose to forget those things because, well, it seems optional.

185
00:17:42,495 --> 00:17:43,456
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how it presents itself.

186
00:17:43,956 --> 00:17:47,296
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there is no immediate punishment that you feel.

187
00:17:47,416 --> 00:17:49,997
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you do, you don't make the association between the two.

188
00:17:52,554 --> 00:18:00,380
[SPEAKER_01]: And then also, because, see, like, if I live under a constant threat, or if I could get in trouble, well, that's very unpleasant for me.

189
00:18:01,401 --> 00:18:03,222
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not a nice state of mind.

190
00:18:03,322 --> 00:18:06,584
[SPEAKER_01]: And plus, these animals are now agitated, because I don't let them eat what they want.

191
00:18:07,345 --> 00:18:17,852
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as I said, naturally, a person would choose a path of less resistance, and then the debt and the punishment will accumulate, and when it comes, you will have nothing but to just cry about it.

192
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:38,052
[SPEAKER_03]: With the simile of, like, your sister, there's also, like, that we were talking on Telegram about, like, how, you know, the otherness of of the mind is like the otherness of people in, like...

